://www.rwu.edu/who-we-are/diversity-equity-inclusion . The Cummings School of Architecture offers an array of undergraduate, graduate and professional degree programs, undergraduate minor and graduate certificate programs in Architecture, Art and Architectural History, Preservation Practices, Real Estate, Urban and Regional Planning, and Urban Studies. Advisement for dual degrees, degree(s) + minor(s), and graduate degree + graduate certificates is widely available. The Cummings School was re-dedicated in 2022 following a major gift from the Cummings Foundation. Job Description: Spring 2027 REAL 501 Real Estate, Equity and Environment --online Fulfills requirements in the MS in Real Estate and Graduate Certificate in Real Estate. 3 credit hours. Asynchronous online Real 510 Real Estate Case Studies and Project Proposal--online Fulfills requirements in the MS in Real Estate and Graduate Certificate in Real Estate. 3 credit hours. Asynchronous online REAL 531 Integrated Project Management &  Technology--online Fulfills requirements in the MS in Real Estate and Graduate Certificate in Real Estate. 3 credit hours. Asynchronous online For additional information regarding the positions above, please contact: Stephen White, AIA, Dean swhite@rwu.edu (401) 254-3607 Requirements: For Real Estate Courses A graduate degree in Real Estate, Business or Law is ideal. Previous teaching experience preferred, including engaging students from varying educational levels. At the University's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be accepted where the candidate can demonstrate, to the satisfaction of the University, an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position. Additional Information: Roger Williams University is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and committed to a diverse workforce. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, or any other basis protected by applicable state and federal law. For information on our Non-discrimination policy, visit here . RWU prohibits all forms of discrimination on the basis of sex in its education programs and activities and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 (Title IX) and its implementing regulations not to discriminate in such a manner. Complaints of Title IX sexual harassment should be reported to the Title IX Coordinator at the contact information listed below. Details regarding the formal complaint process can be found here: Title IX Sexual Harassment Policy and Procedures . All complaints of sexual harassment will be taken seriously and responded to promptly. TITLE IX COORDINATOR : Dr. Jen Stanley, 1 Old Ferry Road, Bristol, RI 02809 / Phone Number: (401) 254-3123 /Email Address: jstanley@rwu.edu Application Instructions: Please attach a resume, cover letter, and list of three (3) professional references. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 1 Old Ferry Road, Bristol, RI 02809"
