y to teach basic, undergraduate courses in subjects that may include the following topical content areas: Computer Applications Construction Estimating and Scheduling Building Systems Contract Administration OPM Project Services Project Communications and Controls Assignment of course schedules will be flexible to accommodate working professionals. Requirements: The qualified applicant will hold a B.S. degree in Construction Management, Architecture, Civil Engineering, or related field with a minimum of five (5) years of experience in the US Construction Industry. Preferred Qualifications The qualified applicant will preferably hold a masters degree in Construction Management, Architecture, Civil Engineering, or related field At the University's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be accepted where the candidate can demonstrate, to the satisfaction of the University, an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position. Additional Information: Roger Williams University is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and committed to a diverse workforce. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, or any other basis protected by applicable state and federal law. For information on our Non-discrimination policy, visit here . RWU prohibits all forms of discrimination on the basis of sex in its education programs and activities and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 (Title IX) and its implementing regulations not to discriminate in such a manner. Complaints of Title IX sexual harassment should be reported to the Title IX Coordinator at the contact information listed below. Details regarding the formal complaint process can be found here: Title IX Sexual Harassment Policy and Procedures . All complaints of sexual harassment will be taken seriously and responded to promptly. TITLE 