    "https://rwu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=190983": {
      "title": "Catering Attendant, p/t - Dining Services",
      "description": "Roger Williams University\nJob Posting: Catering Attendant, p/t - Dining Services Roger Williams University \n\tJob Posting: Catering Attendant, p/t - Dining Services Title Home Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Catering Attendant, p/t - Dining Services Category: Dining Services Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Dining Services Locations: Bristol, RI Posted: Jul 29, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Regular Ref. No.: 1158 Position ID: 190983 Share About Roger Williams University: At Roger Williams University, students are prepared to be thinkers and doers ready to solve challenging problems with innovative solutions. RWU offers 50 majors and robust offerings of graduate and professional programs across eight schools of study including Rhode Island's only law school, with campuses on the coast of Bristol and in the heart of Providence, R.I. With small classrooms and a focus on undergraduate and graduate research and community engagement, a Roger Williams education blends the strength of liberal arts and professional studies, providing all students with the depth and breadth of interdisciplinary thinking and well-rounded knowledge necessary to succeed in our interconnected, global world. RWU is committed to strengthening society through engaged scholarship so that students graduate with the ability to think critically and apply the practical skills that today's employers demand. Roger Williams University seeks to recruit and support a broadly diverse community of faculty and staff. We value all races, genders, identities, and abilities. RWU is committed to creating a thriving community that encourages lifelong learning, professional development, and academic innovation. Job Description: The Catering Service Attendant prepares and serves food at scheduled functions under the supervision of the Catering Manager. This position is primarily responsible for set up, service, break down and clean up of multiple functions or areas on campus. General Standards Interact professionally with other employees, customers, and suppliers. Perform quality work within deadlines, with or without direct supervision. Work effectively as a team leader on all assignments. Work independently while understanding the necessity for communicating and coordinating work efforts with other employees and organizations. Sanitation Maintain sanitation and orderliness of all equipment, supplies and utensils within work area. Set up and Preparation Ensure that all necessary food items have identifiers or menus, displayed in a clean and consistent manner. Set up buffet tables as well as food, beverage, and service items according to pre-established Great Expectations Catering standards. Handle food items appropriately during preparation. Housekeeping Service Clean tables and chairs before, during, and after meal service, as assigned. Clean workstation thoroughly before leaving the area for other assignments. Keep display equipment, buffets, and tables clean and free of debris during meal service, as assigned. Break down events by cleaning and packing unused food dishes, utensils. and equipment for safe removal to appropriate locations. Handle trash and waste properly per unit standards. Customer Service Greet customers courteously, and interact with customers in a manner to ensure customer satisfaction. Interact with customers and resolve customer complaints in a friendly and service oriented manner. Relay relevant comments from customers directly to supervisors. Represent the University in a courteous, efficient, and friendly manner in all customer and employee interactions. Serve customer food and beverage orders quickly, in proper portions, and in a courteous demeanor. Food Preparation Handles foods items appropriately during preparation. Compliance Ensure proper presentation, portion control, and maintenance of proper serving temperatures according to HACCP standards. Utilize all Personal Protective Equipment per dining guidelines, including but not limited to wearing a cut resistance glove whenever using a sharp or potentially sharp tool or instrument. Menu and Catering Assemble and deliver all food and supplies for catered functions to the scheduled locations. Demonstrate a complete understanding of menu items and explain same to customers accurately. Consistently exhibit the ability to keep up with catering delivery schedules and does so calmly, accurately, and efficiently. Additional Functions This position does not directly supervise anyone but is responsible for working with a team and to complete tasks in a group setting. PT Dining $250 signing bonus after a 4-month satisfactory probationary period is completed ** Generous paid holidays, vacation, and sick time, free gym membership, free meals during working hours, free uniforms, free parking, paid employee referral program and 403(b) ** Requirements: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily.  The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required.  Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.  Ability to interact with diverse and high volume customer base in a friendly and efficient manner.  Ability to use the time clock system properly, and record worked hours for processing.  Ability to work at times with minimal supervision, and accomplish tasks without directs instruction, and at times problem solve for the best solution.  Ability to answer basic questions regarding unit operations and direct other questions to appropriate parties.  Possess the ability to meet Dining unit specific uniform standards for this position.  Utilize all Personal Protective Equipment's per dining guidelines.  Wear a cut resistance glove whenever using a sharp or potentially sharp tool or instrument.  Ability to follow all Dining's health and safety standards and requirements.  Must have a valid driver's license and a driver's record in good standing At the University's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be accepted where the candidate can demonstrate, to the satisfaction of the University, an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position. Additional Information: Roger Williams University is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and committed to a diverse workforce. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, or any other basis protected by applicable state and federal law. For information on our Non-discrimination policy, visit here . RWU prohibits all forms of discrimination on the basis of sex in its education programs and activities and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 (Title IX) and its implementing regulations not to discriminate in such a manner. Complaints of Title IX sexual harassment should be reported to the Title IX Coordinator at the contact information listed below. Details regarding the formal complaint process can be found here: Title IX Sexual Harassment Policy and Procedures . All complaints of sexual harassment will be taken seriously and responded to promptly. TITLE IX COORDINATOR : Dr. Jen Stanley, 1 Old Ferry Road, Bristol, RI 02809 / Phone Number: (401) 254-3123 /Email Address: jstanley@rwu.edu Application Instructions: Please attach a resume, cover letter, and list of three (3) professional references. For more information about our Dining Services opportunities, please call our informational help line at: 401.254.3460 or email us at commonsdiningwork@rwu.edu. A manager will be in contact with you. Thank you! Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 1 Old Ferry Road, Bristol, RI 02809"
    },
    "https://rwu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=191015": {
      "title": "Cook, f/t - Dining Services",
      "description": "Roger Williams University\nJob Posting: Cook, f/t - Dining Services Roger Williams University \n\tJob Posting: Cook, f/t - Dining Services Title Home Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Cook, f/t - Dining Services Category: Dining Services Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Dining Services Locations: Bristol, RI Posted: Jul 29, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Regular Ref. No.: 1162 Position ID: 191015 Share About Roger Williams University: At Roger Williams University, students are prepared to be thinkers and doers ready to solve challenging problems with innovative solutions. RWU offers 50 majors and robust offerings of graduate and professional programs across eight schools of study including Rhode Island's only law school, with campuses on the coast of Bristol and in the heart of Providence, R.I. With small classrooms and a focus on undergraduate and graduate research and community engagement, a Roger Williams education blends the strength of liberal arts and professional studies, providing all students with the depth and breadth of interdisciplinary thinking and well-rounded knowledge necessary to succeed in our interconnected, global world. RWU is committed to strengthening society through engaged scholarship so that students graduate with the ability to think critically and apply the practical skills that today's employers demand. Roger Williams University seeks to recruit and support a broadly diverse community of faculty and staff. We value all races, genders, identities, and abilities. RWU is committed to creating a thriving community that encourages lifelong learning, professional development, and academic innovation. Job Description: The culinary cook is responsible for the proper preparation, cooking technique, station setup, and execution of menu items and daily café specials. The culinary work in this position must follow Dining's commitments to sustainability, proper health and safety guidelines and allergy training standards. Essential Functions/Characteristics Interacts professionally with other employees, customers, and suppliers. Performs quality work within deadlines with or without direct supervision. Works effectively as a team contributor on all assignments. Works independently while understanding the necessity for communicating and coordinating work efforts with other employees and organizations. Cooks food based on recipes, guidelines and proper culinary techniques. Cleaning Services Cleans work areas, equipment and utensils, distributes supplies, utensils, and portable equipment. Compliance Assist in the implementation and follow up of proper food safety and sanitation practices in accordance with the RI Food code. Assures compliance with all HACCP food safety requirements. Interacts with co-workers to ensure compliance with company service standards, and inventory and cash control procedures. Assures compliance with all allergy training procedures. Customer Service Serves customers in an efficient and friendly manner, resolves customer concerns seeking assistance from supervisors or management as needed. Food Preparation Ensures that all food is properly cooked, garnished and served. Follows all food production standards including understanding of production metrics. Understand importance of guest count, small batch cooking, reducing waste. Knowledge of all cooking cooking techniques, such as, grilling, baking, broiling, steaming, frying, sautéing. Knowledge of all coking equipment. Utilizes approved food production standards to ensure proper quality, serving temperatures and standard portion control. Able to work all cook stations in upper commons. Set up and Preparation Ensures that all stations and condiments are set-up in time for service. Properly stores foods in designated areas following wrapping, dating, and rotation procedures. Additional Functions This position does not directly supervise anyone but is responsible for working in a team and completing tasks in a group setting. This position is responsible for training of new staff members. FT Dining $500 signing bonus after a 4-month satisfactory probationary period is completed. ** Competitive salary and excellent benefits package including health, dental, paid holidays, free parking, free meals during working hours, free uniforms, free gym membership, tuition benefits, paid employee referral program, and a generous 403(b) match ** Requirements: To perform this job successfully, an individual must be able to perform each essential duty satisfactorily. The requirements listed below are representative of the knowledge, skill, and/or ability required. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions. Strong passion and motivation to create great food. Culinary knowledge of basic kitchen practices, protocols and procedures. At least 2 years working in a high volume restaurant kitchen, or similar working experience. Understanding of typical culinary units of measure. Ability to work safely with large volume culinary equipment including but not limited to slicer, large quantity mixer, robo coupe, tilt skillet, kettle, griddle, combi and convection ovens. Possess the ability to meet Dining unit specific uniform standards for this position. Utilize all Personal Protective Equipment's per dining guidelines. Wear a cut resistant glove whenever using a sharp or potentially sharp tool or instrument.  Ability to follow all of Dining's health and safety standards and requirements. Preferred Qualifications Not applicable At the University's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be excepted where the candidate can demonstrate, to the satisfaction of the University, an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position. Additional Information: Roger Williams University is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and committed to a diverse workforce. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, or any other basis protected by applicable state and federal law. For information on our Non-discrimination policy, visit here . RWU prohibits all forms of discrimination on the basis of sex in its education programs and activities and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 (Title IX) and its implementing regulations not to discriminate in such a manner. Complaints of Title IX sexual harassment should be reported to the Title IX Coordinator at the contact information listed below. Details regarding the formal complaint process can be found here: Title IX Sexual Harassment Policy and Procedures . All complaints of sexual harassment will be taken seriously and responded to promptly. TITLE IX COORDINATOR : Dr. Jen Stanley, 1 Old Ferry Road, Bristol, RI 02809 / Phone Number: (401) 254-3123 /Email Address: jstanley@rwu.edu Application Instructions: Please attach a resume, cover letter, and list of three (3) professional references. For more information about our Dining Services opportunities, please call our informational help line at: 401.254.3460 or email us at commonsdiningwork@rwu.edu . A manager will be in contact with you. Thank you! Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 1 Old Ferry Road, Bristol, RI 02809"
    },
