plete understanding of departmental requirements and interprets their intent accurately to staff members. Maintains sick line and fills open positions. Monitors customer traffic/buying trends and makes appropriate adjustments to improve service deliver. Monitors daily performance and productivity of staff and ensures compliance with established timetables and quality standards. Posts schedule on a weekly basis. Routinely inspects areas of assigned responsibility and reports all substandard safety, security, or equipment conditions to Cash Operations Manager. Schedules employee time off according to established union contract. Trains staff as assigned, and assists with orientation of new employees in a timely and efficient manner. Retail Operations Compiles weekly inventory of all point of sale coolers, racks and walk in coolers. Counts, verifies and reconciles daily sales, following all cash handling standards. Set up and Preparation Carries pans, kettles, and trays of food to and from workstations, stove, and refrigerator. Inventories supplies daily and requisitions items as needed to meet par levels. Additional Functions Monitors customer traffic/buying trends and makes appropriate adjustments to improve service delivery. Maintains sick line and fill open positions. Posts schedule on weekly basis. Under the direction of the Cash Operations Manager, schedules employee time off according to established union contract. Trains staff as assigned, and assists with orientation of new employees in a timely and efficient manner. Confidentiality extends to all matters involving the University, its agents or employees and must use professional judgment in disseminating information as part executing specific job responsibilities. FT Dining $500 signing bonus after a 4-month satisfactory probationary period is completed. ** Competitive salary and excellent benefits package including health, dental, paid holidays, free parking, free meals during working hours, free uniforms, fr