    "https://rwu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202821": {
      "title": "Energy Controls Technician I, Facilities Management",
      "description": "Roger Williams University\nJob Posting: Energy Controls Technician I, Facilities Management Roger Williams University \n\tJob Posting: Energy Controls Technician I, Facilities Management Title Home Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Energy Controls Technician I, Facilities Management Category: Facilities Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Management Locations: Bristol, RI Posted: Jul 21, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Regular Ref. No.: 1088 Position ID: 202821 Share About Roger Williams University: At Roger Williams University, students are prepared to be thinkers and doers ready to solve challenging problems with innovative solutions. RWU offers 50 majors and robust offerings of graduate and professional programs across eight schools of study including Rhode Island's only law school, with campuses on the coast of Bristol and in the heart of Providence, R.I. With small classrooms and a focus on undergraduate and graduate research and community engagement, a Roger Williams education blends the strength of liberal arts and professional studies, providing all students with the depth and breadth of interdisciplinary thinking and well-rounded knowledge necessary to succeed in our interconnected, global world. RWU is committed to strengthening society through engaged scholarship so that students graduate with the ability to think critically and apply the practical skills that today's employers demand. Roger Williams University seeks to recruit and support a broadly diverse community of faculty and staff. We value all races, genders, identities, and abilities. RWU is committed to creating a thriving community that encourages lifelong learning, professional development, and academic innovation. To learn more about Roger Williams University's commitment and support of diversity and inclusion, please visit https://www.rwu.edu/who-we-are/diversity-equity-inclusion . Job Description: To review on a daily basis the operation of the Energy Management System computers to maintain appropriate HVAC and other energy control operations throughout the University. Air Quality Ensures proper building air quality and air balancing to HVAC systems. Construction Plans Reviews new construction plans pertaining to HVAC systems and controls. Corrective Action Initiates corrective action on received heat/cold ventilation complaints throughout the University. Installation Installs new control system points and HVAC equipment as specified by the Mechanical & Electrical Supervisor. Maintenance Maintains and tests all related Energy Management System and control equipment plus repairs and calibrates as needed. Operations Reviews the daily operation of the Energy Management System computers and adjusts building HVAC operating schedules to reflect weekly occupancy variations. Programming Assisted by assigned Supervisor, writes computer programs to minimize and document energy consumption. Record Maintenance Assists assigned Supervisor to initiate and maintain records for an effective computer generated preventive maintenance program. System Upgrade Maintains \"as built drawings\", updates software and building documentation pertaining to HVAC systems and EMS controls. Assists assigned Supervisor in projects to upgrade and modify existing building HVAC systems. Trouble Shooting Performs and initiates trouble shooting and repair to energy management, digital and pneumatic control systems \"points\" and data gathering (DDC controls) panels. Additional Functions Master Energy Controls Technician may provide direction to Journeymen and Apprentice Energy Controls Technician as it pertains to the specific EMS project. The Journeyman Energy Controls Technician may provide direction to the Apprentice Energy Controls Technician as it pertains to the specific EMS project. This is a full-time (40-hour) Facilities Management Union position. $500 signing bonus after a 4-month probationary period is completed ** Competitive salary and excellent benefits package including health, dental, 15 paid holidays, tuition benefits, and a generous  403(b) match ** Requirements: Must have prior ten years' experience in HVAC equipment and controls. Possess a full knowledge of energy management computer programming with a background in Johnson Controls Metasys or equivalent DDC controls system. Possesses a working knowledge associated with a Master ECT or electronics, pneumatic and electrical systems. Must have five (5) years experience commissioning and programming digital controls. Must hold a current Rhode Island telecommunications/data journeyman license or above. A current Rhode Island refrigeration and/or Rhode Island pipe fitter journeyman license/certification or Rhode Island journeyman electrician license is preferred. Must have five (5) years of experience in a commercial/corporate type setting maintaining an Energy Management System. Must be extremely proficient in interpreting and understanding building drawings and documentation. Perform any and all tasks required of the position without assistance and in a timely manner. Must also demonstrate to the reasonable satisfaction of management, the ability to provide expert guidance, direction and remediation to apprentice and/or journeyman Energy Controls Technicians. At the University's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be accepted where the candidate can demonstrate, to the satisfaction of the University, an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position. Additional Information: Roger Williams University is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and committed to a diverse workforce. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, or any other basis protected by applicable state and federal law. For information on our Non-discrimination policy, visit here . RWU prohibits all forms of discrimination on the basis of sex in its education programs and activities and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 (Title IX) and its implementing regulations not to discriminate in such a manner. Complaints of Title IX sexual harassment should be reported to the Title IX Coordinator at the contact information listed below. Details regarding the formal complaint process can be found here: Title IX Sexual Harassment Policy and Procedures . All complaints of sexual harassment will be taken seriously and responded to promptly. TITLE IX COORDINATOR : Dr. Jen Stanley, 1 Old Ferry Road, Bristol, RI 02809 / Phone Number: (401) 254-3123 /Email Address: jstanley@rwu.edu Application Instructions: Please attach a resume, cover letter, and list of three (3) professional references. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 1 Old Ferry Road, Bristol, RI 02809"
    },
    "https://rwu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204861": {
      "title": "Refrigeration/Appliance/HVAC Technician I, Facilities Management",
      "description": "Roger Williams University\nJob Posting: Refrigeration/Appliance/HVAC Technician I, Facilities Management Roger Williams University \n\tJob Posting: Refrigeration/Appliance/HVAC Technician I, Facilities Management Title Home Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Refrigeration/Appliance/HVAC Technician I, Facilities Management Category: Facilities Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Management Locations: Bristol, RI Posted: Sep 16, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Regular Ref. No.: 1102 Position ID: 204861 Share About Roger Williams University: At Roger Williams University, students are prepared to be thinkers and doers ready to solve challenging problems with innovative solutions. RWU offers 50 majors and robust offerings of graduate and professional programs across eight schools of study including Rhode Island's only law school, with campuses on the coast of Bristol and in the heart of Providence, R.I. With small classrooms and a focus on undergraduate and graduate research and community engagement, a Roger Williams education blends the strength of liberal arts and professional studies, providing all students with the depth and breadth of interdisciplinary thinking and well-rounded knowledge necessary to succeed in our interconnected, global world. RWU is committed to strengthening society through engaged scholarship so that students graduate with the ability to think critically and apply the practical skills that today's employers demand. Roger Williams University seeks to recruit and support a broadly diverse community of faculty and staff. We value all races, genders, identities, and abilities. RWU is committed to creating a thriving community that encourages lifelong learning, professional development, and academic innovation. To learn more about Roger Williams University's commitment and support of diversity and inclusion, please visit https://www.rwu.edu/who-we-are/diversity-equity-inclusion . Job Description: Analyze, repair and maintain ventilation and air conditioning systems. Equipment Evacuate and recharge system. Remove freon from system by means of a recovery machine. HVAC When required will work with the Energy Management Technicians on resolving HVAC related issues. Installations Installs, inspects, operates and repairs appliances and HVAC equipment using necessary hand tools and testing equipment. Repairs Repairs freon leaks and retest for freon leaks. Upgrades Assist the Manager of Mechanical and Electrical Systems and the Mechanical, Electrical, Plumbing Systems Supervisor in projects to upgrade and modify existing building HVAC systems. Requirements: Technical school training and minimum 5 years' experience. Must be licensed to purchase and recover refrigerant in the State of Rhode Island. Must hold current RI refrigeration and/or RI pipe fitter Journeyman license. Must have 5 years' experience in a corporate/commercial type setting, maintaining HVAC systems. Must be extremely proficient in interpreting and understanding building drawings and documentation. Perform any and all tasks required of the position without assistance and in a timely manner. Must also demonstrate to the reasonable satisfaction of management, the ability to provide expert guidance, direction and remediation to levels III and/or II Refrigeration/Appliance/HVAC Technicians. At the University's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be accepted where the candidate can demonstrate, to the satisfaction of the University, an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position. Additional Information: Roger Williams University is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and committed to a diverse workforce. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, or any other basis protected by applicable state and federal law. For information on our Non-discrimination policy, visit here . RWU prohibits all forms of discrimination on the basis of sex in its education programs and activities and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 (Title IX) and its implementing regulations not to discriminate in such a manner. Complaints of Title IX sexual harassment should be reported to the Title IX Coordinator at the contact information listed below. Details regarding the formal complaint process can be found here: Title IX Sexual Harassment Policy and Procedures . All complaints of sexual harassment will be taken seriously and responded to promptly. TITLE IX COORDINATOR : Dr. Jen Stanley, 1 Old Ferry Road, Bristol, RI 02809 / Phone Number: (401) 254-3123 /Email Address: jstanley@rwu.edu Application Instructions: Please attach a resume, cover letter, and list of three (3) professional references. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 1 Old Ferry Road, Bristol, RI 02809"
