    "https://rwu.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205949": {
      "title": "Senior Research Manager, HousingWorks RI",
      "description": "Roger Williams University\nJob Posting: Senior Research Manager, HousingWorks RI Roger Williams University \n\tJob Posting: Senior Research Manager, HousingWorks RI Title Home Employment Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Senior Research Manager, HousingWorks RI Category: Professional and Clerical Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: HousingWorks RI, ES Locations: Providence, RI Posted: Oct 20, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Regular Ref. No.: 2785 Position ID: 205949 Share About Roger Williams University: At Roger Williams University, students are prepared to be thinkers and doers ready to solve challenging problems with innovative solutions. RWU offers 50 majors and robust offerings of graduate and professional programs across eight schools of study including Rhode Island's only law school, with campuses on the coast of Bristol and in the heart of Providence, R.I. With small classrooms and a focus on undergraduate and graduate research and community engagement, a Roger Williams education blends the strength of liberal arts and professional studies, providing all students with the depth and breadth of interdisciplinary thinking and well-rounded knowledge necessary to succeed in our interconnected, global world. RWU is committed to strengthening society through engaged scholarship so that students graduate with the ability to think critically and apply the practical skills that today's employers demand. Roger Williams University seeks to recruit and support a broadly diverse community of faculty and staff. We value all races, genders, identities, and abilities. RWU is committed to creating a thriving community that encourages lifelong learning, professional development, and academic innovation. To learn more about Roger Williams University's commitment and support of diversity and inclusion, please visit https://www.rwu.edu/who-we-are/diversity-equity-inclusion . Job Description: Reporting to the Executive Director, HousingWorks RI, the Senior Research Manager is responsilbe for managing all aspects of research and data analysis to inform public policy and promote dialogue about the relationship between housing and the state's economic future. The Senior Research Manager works in close partnership with all other HousingWorks RI affiliates, members of the Roger Williams University community, as well as internal and external partners, and policy organizations. Research and Policy Research and write reports including the annual HWRI housing fact book, issue briefs and special reports on housing, and website blogs. Manage all analysis of housing and economic data to support development of HWRI publications. Make public presentations to local, state, and federal constituency groups, policymakers and the media. Oversee all research and policy fellows and interns engaged with HousingWorks RI and the Latino Policy Institute. Collaborate with faculty on research and data analysis. Guest lecture at courses at the University, as required. Serve as spokesperson on complex data analysis when necessary. Engage Advisory Board members in the research conducted at HousingWorks RI. Fund Development Identify potential funding sources to support HWRI research. Work with Institutional Advancement to assist in writing grant proposals and nurture potential funders. Identify internal and external collaboration opportunities for national research grants. Assist the Director, HousingWorks in writing any reports/evaluations required by funders. Additional Functions Support all activities associated with the University. Participate in committees and other projects, activities, or assignments as directed. This is a grant-funded position that is contingent upon the existence and availability of external funding. Requirements: Bachelor's degree in a related field. Five years' related work experience in policy analysis and research. Five years' experience in managing a team of interns and consultants in a collaborative environment. Ability and experience in managing multiple projects and deadlines Expertise with Rhode Island and federal data sources, and US Census reports (American Community Survey, PUMS Files, Decennial Census, Population Estimates program, Manufacturing, Construction and Mining Statistics, Housing Survey, and others). Demonstrated strong analytical and statistical skills and experience with statistical applications such as DataFerrett, SAS, and/or SPSS. Ability to translate data, statistical information, and concepts into graphical representations. Excellent written and oral communication skills. Advanced skills and knowledge of Microsoft Office applications. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree in a related field. Experience with social media and use of the web as a communications tool. Experience communicating effectively with a diverse group including peers, senior officials, and members of the media. Knowledge of how housing policy intersects with other issue areas such as education, health, and the economy. At the University's discretion, the education and experience prerequisites may be accepted where the candidate can demonstrate, to the satisfaction of the University, an equivalent combination of education and experience specifically preparing the candidate for success in the position. Additional Information: Roger Williams University is an affirmative action/equal opportunity employer and committed to a diverse workforce. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, or any other basis protected by applicable state and federal law. For information on our Non-discrimination policy, visit here . RWU prohibits all forms of discrimination on the basis of sex in its education programs and activities and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 (Title IX) and its implementing regulations not to discriminate in such a manner. Complaints of Title IX sexual harassment should be reported to the Title IX Coordinator at the contact information listed below. Details regarding the formal complaint process can be found here: Title IX Sexual Harassment Policy and Procedures . All complaints of sexual harassment will be taken seriously and responded to promptly. TITLE IX COORDINATOR : Dr. Jen Stanley, 1 Old Ferry Road, Bristol, RI 02809 / Phone Number: (401) 254-3123 /Email Address: jstanley@rwu.edu Application Instructions: Please attach a resume, cover letter, and list of three (3) professional references. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 1 Old Ferry Road, Bristol, RI 02809"
